{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120041","id":4600991521,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEj2PIQ","number":120041,"title":"Theme Base Color affects Viewport in HDR 2D with Light3D Shadows in Compatibility","user":{"login":"MrSolaire810","id":184316402,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvxx8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184316402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810","html_url":"https://github.com/MrSolaire810","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrSolaire810/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-06-06T00:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T02:04:31Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.6.stable, 4.6.3.stable, 4.7.beta5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Windows 10 (build 19044) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 580 2048SP (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21924.61) - AMD Ryzen 5 5500 (12 threads) - 31.87 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe viewport window of the editor gets oversaturated when adding 2 or more Light3D nodes with Shadows turned on. When changing the editor's parameter <interface/theme/base_color>, it seems to subtract that color from the viewport, giving the scene a purple hue with my settings despite all the colors of the Light3D nodes being white and no environment.\nThis only happens in the Compatibility renderer.\n\n#### Screenshots\n| HDR 2D Off | HDR 2D On |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f3846e3-11a1-4cae-81fd-ec67eb44b887\" /> | <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f99f9240-392b-4500-a236-86bddb382dcd\" /> |\n| Base Theme HDR 2D Off | Base Theme HDR 2D On |\n| <img width=\"1920\" height=\"1037\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3249ed14-5f6e-49ae-af93-e9babef7be62\" /> | <img width=\"1918\" height=\"1035\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5aea055-98c9-4fa5-b718-fa8f69f6fd74\" /> |\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a Project.\n2. Change Renderer to Compatibility.\n3. Add a MeshInstance3D with a Plane mesh.\n4. Add 2 or more Light3D Nodes. (OmniLight3D, SpotLight3D, etc)\n5. Turn On Shadows in those Nodes.\n6. Turn On HDR 2D in Project Settings.\n7. Change Base Color in Editor Settings\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28667391/MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120041/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}